On Jun 1, 2007, at 5:50 PM, Lei Wu wrote:

> Thanks again! I must miss some important thing in JRI. How can I  
> get the R feed back if I initialize the Rengine as Rengine re = new  
> Rengine(args, false, new TextConsole2())? I don't want user to type  
> anything as the input to R. I will feed the R command from my  
> program. But I do want to see the output from running my R command.
>

"R feed back"? What do you mean? If you want to run R without the  
event loop, new Rengine(args, false, null) is quite sufficient (no  
need for TextConsole). Everything then works exactly as in Rserve,  
i.e. you get all your results directly from eval. The callbacks are  
used when you want to run the full REPL like a console.

Cheers,
Simon


